// Generated guardian art — ALL 18 COMBOS (Nov 22, 2026, Derek: "Can you fix it so it accepts them?").
// Layered, not baked composites: 18 figures cut out from their white
// backgrounds (PIL: near-white >238 connected to the border, plus large
// enclosed white gaps like the bow triangle, dilate 1px, feather sigma 0.8,
// trimmed and resized to 600px tall) as transparent WebP q70, plus the 3
// detailed class backgrounds once, at 900px wide WebP q70. Figures total
// 457 KB, backgrounds 127 KB, base64 ~780 KB. The app renders the
// background + the cut-out figure layered, so the 3 backgrounds are shared
// instead of baked into every picture. Skin is baked into these pictures:
// Skin works on these pictures too: GeneratedGuardian recolors the
// figure's face + hands on a canvas (lib/generatedSkin), so Armor/Onboarding
// keep the Skin picker visible while Generated is on. Build, colors, gem and
// cape are baked in and do not change the generated picture. Known flaw, carried over from the composites:
// the Ranger arrow-tip glow and the Spellweaver star glow have a hard-edged
// pale disc behind them — the soft glow faded into the white background
// before cut-out. A real host (R2 bucket active-life-quest-videos, Derek
// must create it in the Cloudflare dashboard) would still be needed for
// full-resolution originals or any new pictures; this embedded set is the
// fix that fits inside the Workers bundle. SVG GuardianAvatar stays the
// default and the fallback.

